  "body": "No pick reaches the 4-axis generator for a die opening with different top and bottom outlines:\n- edge chains: \"a profile stitched from 9 open runs at Z20.000 is not supported - pick one face or closed edge chain on that plane\";\n- faces: \"Face 6 of 'sam' has 2 closed rings - a profile is one ring; pick the edge chain of the ring to cut\" (the ring IS several chains, so the two messages send the user in a circle);\n- wall patches: \"Curved face 13 of 'sam' is not a profile\".\n\nBlocks: the Sodick owner's own validation part (15 mm square on top lofted to a 34-lobe flower on the bottom, `sam/sam_edm_part.step`), the twisted square and the round-to-square hole on EDM-T3. 2-axis cuts stitch the same picks fine.\n\nDone means: a face's hole loop, or a stitched closed ring of several chains, is accepted as a 4-axis profile on each plane; the owner's part and EDM-T3's two features generate and verify; pinned by tests.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (spikeypineapple, #617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
